kernora-quickshare (1.0.2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Much less Bluetooth radio time, which can matter for Wi-Fi on cards
    that do Wi-Fi and Bluetooth on one chip (a tester gets ~10 s Wi-Fi
    drops while gaming):
    - the nearby listener scans for Bluetooth LE only. btleplug asked
      bluez for "auto" discovery, which also runs classic inquiry over and
      over, and Quick Share only ever needs LE adverts (patches/btleplug);
    - it only scans while the "someone nearby is sharing" prompt can show
      up: Quick Share on, hidden, Ask when a device nearby is sharing on.
      Visible to everyone, the prompt turned off or Quick Share off means
      no scanning at all;
    - stopping the listener actually stops the bluez scan now.

 -- Kernora Developers <developers@kernora.invalid>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0700

kernora-quickshare (1.0.1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Notifications say what ChromeOS says: "Receive with Quick Share?",
    "Pixel is sharing an image with you." plus the secure connection ID,
    "Receiving / Sending ... from / to ...", "Image received from ...",
    "Failed to send ...", "Device nearby is sharing" with Enable and
    Dismiss. The progress goes away by itself when it's done.
  * A single received image gets Copy to clipboard (wl-copy).
  * A device that can't be reached ends in "Can't share" instead of
    spinning on Connecting forever: rqs_lib reports failed connects now
    (10 s TCP timeout) and the daemon gives up after 25 s; the stale entry
    leaves the device list.
  * Desktop entries use the new org.kernora.quickshare app icon.
  * "Device nearby is sharing" stops nagging (a tester got it every few
    minutes, stacked in history):
    - rqs_lib only reacts to real Quick Share adverts (0xFE2C with the
      FC128E model ID, like ChromeOS), not to every Fast Pair gadget;
    - one notification per sharing phone, gone ~30 s after it stops;
    - Dismiss or closing it keeps it quiet for 15 minutes (ChromeOS);
    - new Don't ask again button turns the prompt off.
  * Quick Share can be switched off completely (SetEnabled), and
    "visible to everyone for 10 minutes" is its own switch
    (SetHighVisibility).

 -- Kernora Developers <developers@kernora.invalid>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0700

kernora-quickshare (1.0.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * First version: Quick Share with Android phones and other computers,
    built on rqs_lib from rquickshare (the core Packet uses). Incoming
    files ask first, show the PIN and land in Downloads.

 -- Kernora Developers <developers@kernora.invalid>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:00:00 -0700
